        "execSummary":  "Silent agent failures ΓÇö where an agent appears to succeed but returns wrong results ΓÇö are among the hardest operational risks to manage in production AI systems, and AWS\u0027s AgentCore insights feature directly targets this gap. For enterprise leaders deploying agents in customer-support or operations contexts, the ability to detect and rank behavioral failures without waiting for users to report them is a meaningful step toward meeting reliability SLAs. The shift from reactive debugging of individual traces to proactive identification of systemic failure patterns changes how agent ops teams should be structured and staffed. Organizations not yet on Bedrock AgentCore should evaluate whether their current observability stack has equivalent silent-failure detection, as this is rapidly becoming a table-stakes capability.",
