        "summary":  "Model Context Protocol (MCP) is shifting to a stateless architecture so every request carries all the information needed for any server to process it independently, eliminating the requirement for servers to maintain session state. This dramatically simplifies production deployment across distributed cloud infrastructure and brings MCP in line with cloud-native application patterns enterprises already use at scale.",
        "execSummary":  "MCP\u0027s move to stateless design removes one of the biggest friction points blocking enterprises from deploying AI agent infrastructure in production. Previously, stateful sessions meant load balancers and distributed systems had to route requests to specific server instances, creating scaling headaches. Enterprises evaluating agentic platforms should factor this architectural change into their MCP adoption timelines, as it meaningfully reduces operational complexity. The key caveat: stateless MCP is still in design and implementation phase, so pilot deployments should track the stabilization timeline before committing to production rollout.",
