        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "ING\u0027s Global CIO of Wholesale Banking Bouke Hoving explains that successful AI transformation depends on foundational infrastructure, not pilot programs. Banks with modernized platforms and standardized data architectures can move AI initiatives to production quickly, while those lacking governance, data strategy, and scalable foundations remain permanently stuck in pilot phase. Hoving argues that data infrastructure investment is the prerequisite, not the follow-on, to AI success.",
        "execSummary":  "ING\u0027s Global CIO delivers a clear verdict for enterprise leaders: organizations that cannot scale AI beyond pilots are almost always dealing with a data and infrastructure problem, not an AI problem. Hoving\u0027s framework ΓÇö modernize the platform first, standardize the data architecture, then layer AI ΓÇö offers a sequencing model any CIO can pressure-test against their own roadmap. For customer-support leaders, this means AI-powered service transformation requires clean, governed data pipelines before deploying agents or GenAI tools. The implication is sobering: enterprises still in POC cycles a year from now likely need to look upstream at their data foundations, not at their AI tool selections.",
