        "execSummary":  "Bhatt\u0027s practitioner perspective cuts through vendor hype: the hardest part of enterprise AI is the boring operational work of managing cost, latency, and compliance once a pilot is approved for production. For senior leaders, his framing reinforces that AI program velocity is largely a people and governance challenge, not a technology one. Customer-support and operations leaders will recognize the tension he describes ΓÇö business sponsors expect ChatGPT-level speed and zero errors while IT navigates data privacy and cost controls. The actionable takeaway is to set explicit production readiness criteria before pilots start, not after they succeed.",
